+The shared `secure_dma_v2.cmake` fragment exports only device sources and compile definitions;
+it does not reference `../test/` or define `SECURE_DMA_V2_TEST_BINDING`. The repository's root
+`CMakeLists.txt` only includes the device-source contract. It contains no test targets, test options,
+or test-configuration includes. CI needs no `test/`, `stub/`, or `cmake/` directory from this repository.
+Keep the platform's own `ms_kernels/CMakeLists.txt`; this standalone root configuration creates no
+build targets and does not build the device library.
+If CI reports a missing `secure_dma_test_key_binding.cc`, sync the updated fragment and check
+that the platform source list does not separately append that file or `SECURE_DMA_V2_TEST_BINDING`.
+The URMA diagnostic requires no key binding. Encrypted-copy operation still requires the existing
+device key provider; the diagnostic does not replace or supply one.
+
+For the source-copy workflow, the managed block in the platform's `ms_kernels/CMakeLists.txt` is:
+
+```cmake
+include("${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/secure_dma_v2.cmake")
+list(APPEND common_src ${SECURE_DMA_V2_SOURCES})
+if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "^(aarch64|arm64|ARM64)$"
+   OR CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER MATCHES "aarch64")
+    add_compile_definitions(${SECURE_DMA_V2_DEFINES})
+endif()
+```
+
+Keep the platform's existing framework include paths and its `inc`/`src` include directories.
+The copied source set supplies all SecureDma-local headers; `kernel_base.h`, `kernel_log.h`, and
+`kernel_errcode.h` come from the platform framework. The fragment uses the same AArch64 detection
+for AES instruction flags, including the compiler-path fallback. The copy list does not supply
+`ms_kernels/src/secure_dma_test_key_binding.cc`; appending that path requires a separately existing
+platform file and is unnecessary for this URMA probe.
